TYPE UDT_ShredderSequencerStim
  ROOTID 0
  COMMENT "Command and published state of the shredder-sequencer stimulus head. The harness writes the command members before an index starts and reads the published ones while it runs. The head presents a commanded plant to FB_ShredderSequencer through the input map's own test-injection members, so the sequencer sees equipment that behaves to a timeline rather than to a field. THE FEEDBACK MEMBERS ARE CLOSED-LOOP BY DESIGN: the shredder motor block latches a fail-to-run ten seconds after it commands a contactor that does not confirm, and that fault aborts three of the sequencer's step transitions, so a feedback timeline that ignored what the motor was actually commanded would inject aborts no vector asked for. Each modelled contactor answers the output the PLC is really driving, after a delay the vector chooses. Every time is a duration measured from the start of the scenario, which is the instant the head cleardown finishes, never from Start."
  MEMBERS
    Start : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the index start bool. Its rising edge begins the head cleardown; its falling edge does not truncate an index, which ends only by reaching TailEnd."
    ScenarioDone : Bool COMMENT "Out: the index reached TailEnd. Latched, so a harness that was not polling at that instant still sees that it finished."
    EndAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): how long the scenario itself lasts. The three head dwells before it and the three tail dwells after it are the head's own and are not included."
    ResetAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the fault-reset pulse is asserted inside the scenario under ResetMode 1."
    ResetMode : Int COMMENT "In (harness): 0 never asserts the fault reset inside the scenario; 1 pulses it once at ResetAt; 2 holds it true throughout, so an edge-triggered reset finds no edge to act on."
    ResetRequest : Bool COMMENT "Out: this head is asking for the plant fault-reset line. It is a REQUEST and not the line itself, because DB_Controls.FaultReset is shared with the hopper head, the pusher head, the motor block and the pusher block: the head publishes here and one authored rung arbitrates, passing whatever another head wrote through whenever this index is not running."
    ArrivedDirty : Bool COMMENT "Out: a latched cause was already standing when this index began, before the head cleardown had done anything. Not a verdict on the block - a verdict on what the previous index left behind."
    InertAtStart : Bool COMMENT "Out: the head cleardown succeeded and the block held no latched cause when the scenario began. False means the scenario ran against a block that was not clean, so its result says nothing."
    RecoverFailed : Bool COMMENT "Out: a latched cause was still standing after the tail cleardown, so the block could not be returned to rest by a reset - a finding about the block, not about the index."
    InertAtEnd : Bool COMMENT "Out: the tail cleardown left the block with no latched cause, so the next index starts clean."
    Armed : Bool COMMENT "Out: the observation window is open. Published so the copy layer's observation latches are armed by this head's phase and not from the start of the index - a free-running latch would fill from the cleardown, where the block is legitimately being driven."
    ArmAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): start of the observation window, measured from the start of the scenario."
    ArmUntil : Time COMMENT "In (harness): end of the observation window."
    Phase : Int COMMENT "Out: which index phase is running, positional - 1 head disarm, 2 head reset, 3 head verify, 4 scenario, 5 tail disarm, 6 tail reset, 7 tail verify, 0 between indexes. The codes are this head's own; never decode them against another head's."
    PreStartHold : Time COMMENT "In (harness): how long the head holds the plant idle-but-healthy at the start of the scenario before it presses the cycle-start button, so a vector has a settled Step 0 to depart from."
    StartPressWidth : Time COMMENT "In (harness): how long the cycle-start press is held. Many scans wide, so a press cannot fall between two scans and be missed."
    DischargeConfirmDelay : Time COMMENT "In (harness): delay from the sequencer commanding the discharge conveyor to the head confirming it running. Longer than DB_Settings.DischargeConveyorTimeout and Step 20 times out to Idle with its fault latched instead of advancing."
    RevFeedbackDelay : Time COMMENT "In (harness): delay from the reverse output command to the head confirming reverse running. It must stay inside the motor block's fail-to-run window or the motor faults and the step aborts for a reason the vector did not ask for."
    FwdFeedbackDelay : Time COMMENT "In (harness): delay from the forward output command to the head confirming forward running. Same fail-to-run caveat as the reverse delay."
    HopperHighAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the hopper high-level sensor is asserted, from the start of the scenario."
    HopperClearAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the hopper reads clear again. The infeed restart and upstream enable delays run from here."
    StopAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the commanded stop event fires. WHICH stop it is comes from the three levers below, not from this - so no stop-reason value table has to be invented."
    StopByButton : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the stop event is the operator stop button. The only stop reason that also forces the pusher to mode 0, so it is separable from the other two by observation alone."
    StopByDownstreamLoss : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the stop event is loss of the downstream-running permission. It must inhibit the pusher's cycle without taking hand-jog away."
    StopByUnhealthy : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the stop event is loss of the control-circuit healthy input. It reaches the motor block as well, so a vector using it is asserting about two blocks."
    WithholdDischargeConfirm : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): never confirm the discharge conveyor running, whatever the delay says. The direct route to the discharge timeout, with no dependence on comparing two durations."
    WithholdRevFeedback : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): never confirm reverse running. It stalls the reverse step AND makes the motor block latch a fail-to-run after FTTime, so the observable outcome is a two-block outcome."
    WithholdFwdFeedback : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): never confirm forward running. Same two-block caveat as the reverse lever."
    InjectMotorFault : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): assert the field motor-fault input at the stop instant. The only way a vector raises the motor's fault deliberately rather than as a side effect of a withheld feedback."
